A||||0||Fieroguy||Useful tip on strange problems
Z||000000||Fieroguy||07-10-99||07:11 AM||||I thought I would share something which<br>I learned thru much trial and error<br>and at great expense.I had a 85 gt v6 auto<br>and it would lose power very badly sometimes<br>when hot.It would feel like a two cylinder<br>and at other times it would run great.<br>After much parts swapping,ecm,etc. the problem turned out to be hairline cracks<br>in the distributor piece that goes on the<br>shaft.I think they are cracked by being<br>too rough when taking off rotor for <br>replacement.Check this for cracks as<br>it will do serious havoc with your timing.<br>When cold it would run ok but after it<br>warmed up the power would go away.Almost<br>got smoked off a couple of times when<br>I tried to cross highway or something<br>and had a two cylinder instead of v6!!!
